package Physics.Tests

use Libraries.Game.Collision.LocalCollisionPoints3D
use Libraries.Game.Collision.Shapes.Triangle

/*
A box hanging half over the edge of a triangle that covers x >= 0. The
contacts on the overhanging side are cut at the triangle's edge, grown
by its margin, at x = -0.04.

Unless a test says otherwise, the triangle is a large one lying flat
at height 0, from MakeLargeTriangle, with the usual margin of 0.04, so
its thickened surface is at 0.04. The box is 0.5 on each side for
collisions (see RunBox), with no rotation, and the triangle is item A.
A box whose center is at 0.28 has its bottom at 0.03, so it sinks 0.01
into the surface.
*/
class BoxTriangleOverhangTest is PhysicsTest
    on create
        SetName("Box and triangle: hanging over an edge")
    end

    action Run
        Triangle triangle
        triangle:Set(MakeVector(0, 0, 5), MakeVector(0, 0, -5), MakeVector(5, 0, 0))
        triangle:SetMargin(0.04)
        LocalCollisionPoints3D points = RunBox(triangle, MakeTransform(0, 0.28, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0), false)
        CheckWhole("box overhang: four contacts", points:GetPointCount(), 4)
        CheckAllContacts("box overhang", points, 0, -1, 0, -0.01)
        CheckWhole("box overhang: inner corner", CountContactsNear(points, 0.25, 0.03, 0.25), 1)
        CheckWhole("box overhang: cut at the edge", CountContactsNear(points, -0.04, 0.03, 0.25), 1)
        CheckWhole("box overhang: other cut", CountContactsNear(points, -0.04, 0.03, -0.25), 1)
    end
end
